    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The grouping idea helps, but I'm still stuck on the nature of these gaps. They feel less like \"errors\" and more like these tiny, persistent little things that just slip through the cracks every time we update the ledger. It's almost like they are intentionally avoiding the standard filters. If I wanted to characterize these \"nuisance\" entries in a report to my supervisor—without sounding like I'm chasing ghosts—how should I describe the pattern of these small, elusive anomalies?",
